review_comments.body:
@pcbeingused333 
There appears to be a stream-reuse issue here. Close() closes the output pipe reader but does not wait for a producer blocked in the source’s Read() to finish. If Reset() then replaces s.outputWrite, the old goroutine can resume and call s.outputWrite.CloseWithError(err) on the new stream’s pipe, causing that stream to fail.

Could we capture the pipe writer before launching the goroutine and use that same captured writer for both zw.Reset(...) and CloseWithError(...)? A regression test should block the first source reader, call Close() and Reset() with a second source, then unblock the first reader and verify that the second stream remains unaffected.
